WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.003 line:92%
-Sure! My pleasure. My pleasure.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:06.072
-This is truly one of
my favorite movies of the year.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:06.673 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's wonderful.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also -- Before we get to it,
I want to thank you

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:11.811
because you were also nominated
for a Golden Globe.

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:12.779 line:92%
You were in the audience.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:15.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
I made a joke about
it was the first time men

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
could hear their name as
nominees and not be terrified.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.954
And you gave me a great reaction
to that joke,

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:23.957
and I think it got a bigger
laugh than the joke itself.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I got a rubber face,
what can I say?

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got a rubber face.
It was great.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.697 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Well, thank you so much.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.598 line:92%
So, this film, you actually --

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:36.169
It's about families living in
a budget hotel in Florida.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.203 line:92%
It's obviously an actual hotel

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.472 size:88% position:44%
that was still running
while you were shooting.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.073 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right. Right.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:42.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were residents there
around that kind of

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:45.912
were living the same life that
we were depicting in the film.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You play a manager
of this hotel.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were there times
that people who live there

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
thought you were
the actual manager?

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well you know,
like, a couple of times,

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
they had to get us
out of the way

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:56.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they had to
check people in, for example.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:57.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'd be in the middle
of the scene,

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were like,
"Can you move aside?

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got business to do here."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And one of the other things
that was great --

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:06.199
There's a fantastic scene in the
movie where, as the manager,

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:10.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to get actual birds
out of the way.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.641 size:75% position:38%
-These birds were --
They're protected.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.875 line:92%
So you couldn't touch them,

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
and occasionally
they'd come over to --

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:20.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the real manager was
feeding them Cheetos.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's why they would come
around,

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sometimes they'd be
in our shot.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.287 line:92%
And one time the director said,

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Can you deal with that --
those birds?"

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the camera was rolling
and we went with it,

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:35.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I had a little improvised
scene with the birds.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:35.929 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were very good.
-They were great.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're great partners.
-Yeah, great scene partners.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:40.800 line:92%
It was a wonderful scene.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will also say, it seems like
if birds are protected,

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.805 size:78% position:39%
you shouldn't be able
to give them Cheetos.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:46.339 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
That seems like --
-I didn't give them --

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:52.445
-Yeah, no look, it's very clear.
-It's the other guy.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.947 line:92%
-Yeah, throw him under the bus.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:57.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, the kids -- Obviously,
you're a trained actor.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:00.520
The kids and a lot of the actors
in this film

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
came from local
community theaters.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some of them
had not acted before.

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:08.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the --
The mother that plays the --

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:11.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, the mother
and the 6-year-old child

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.565 size:88% position:44% line:92%
are the main performers.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the child is 6 years old.
-Yeah.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.638 size:88% position:44%
-She's done some things,
but she's 6 years old.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:19.072 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:22.942
-And Bria, who plays her mother,
was found on Instagram.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, she's fantastic.
-Fantastic.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:28.748
And I loved performing with them
because they're very free.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have nothing
to compare it to.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:31.818 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They're totally in.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're really good
at pretending.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're really good at just
dealing with what we're doing.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.260
They aren't thinking outside of
what's happening.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're very present,
and that's always a pleasure.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so when you
work with people

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have less experience
than you,

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:49.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
does it make you
feel more experienced,

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
or does it bring you back to
like when you were --

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:52.739 line:92%
-I think it brings you back,

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:54.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's what you
always want to do.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
You kind of want to forget
what you know

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:59.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
and enter the story
on its own terms

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:03.616
and not think about tricks
you have or a process you need.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:07.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, you try to find
new ways.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.688 line:92%
-There are a lot of people

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:11.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are pulling for you
at the Oscars.

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.125 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's cool.

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.526 line:92%
-And one of them is Denis Leary.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
Denis Leary tweeted,
"Really need Willem Dafoe

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:17.497 line:92%
to win an Oscar this year

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:21.301
so I can be mistaken for
an Oscar winner wherever I go."

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.002 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:23.770 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So that was very nice.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it seems
a little self-interested,

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's still --
-It's self-interest.

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and then,
this is pretty great.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.110 line:92%
"This morning my Uber driver

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
said he loved me
in 'The Florida Project'

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:35.815
and wondered if I was working on
my Oscar speech.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:36.616 line:92%
I said thank you and yes.

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:39.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then we took a photo together.
#GoDafoe."

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:40.653 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it is --
It's already happening.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.457
-The only thing -- I got a beef
with Denis Leary

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:48.361
because he keeps on having me
take the rap for "Dumbo Drop."

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:48.795 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, wow.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he was in the movie
"Dumbo Drop"

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:52.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now you have to answer
questions about that?

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, he always says,
"No, that wasn't me.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was Dafoe!"
-Oh, my God!

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:58.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It's even worse.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.172 line:92%
-I've never seen the movie.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:01.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
I shouldn't say it,
until I've seen it.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's true.
I will tell you this.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:03.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's a good movie?

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:06.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If he's getting credit for
"Florida Project,"

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:08.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
you deserve better than
"Dumbo Drop."

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:09.015 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:13.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is there anyone --
Who do you get mistaken for?

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Probably the best one,
and the most --

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:18.391 size:75% position:38%
the one that happens
the most times is --

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:21.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
particularly when I'm thin --
Mick Jagger.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.595 line:92%
-Okay, that's pretty great.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's always
very enthusiastic.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:29.068
They -- It's always, "Oh! Oh!
Mick Jagger! Mick Jagger!"

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:29.602 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:33.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're always like,
"Oh, do that thing! You know?

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.742 line:92%
Come on, baby, do that thing!"

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:39.545 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.914 line:92%
Which is cool. Which is cool.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love Mick Jagger.
-Yeah.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:44.784 line:92%
-I grew up with Mick Jagger.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:48.121
Forget that he's about
20 years older than I am.

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:48.655 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:51.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
You got to let that go.

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:51.557 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He's cool.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:54.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It seems like, because I will
say that was very good.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:55.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems like you own it,
and you don't --

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:58.431 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Do you correct people

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
or do you let them have
that moment and say

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.235 size:78% position:39% line:92%
they met Mick Jagger?

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Better yet --
Once I was someplace --

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:05.371 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it was in Italy,

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:09.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I went to the toilet
and I heard the kitchen going,

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.411 line:92%
"...Mick Jagger. Mick Jagger."

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:15.048
And I get so scared that they'd
come out and ask me

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:16.249 line:92%
for an autograph or something.

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:20.386
I was -- I didn't know whether I
could say, "No, I'm not him."

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or I just do it
and hope I get out

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:25.525
before they really ask me
to dance or sing, you know.

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:28.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The best would be if you were
in Italy and you faked it

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:33.166
and they immediately looked were
like, "He's no Mick Jagger."

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:33.866 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:34.901 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-That's another story.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations.
Good luck at the Oscars.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:42.241
It's just such a fantastic film,
and it's so great to have you.

